---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import Term from '../components/Term.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Doc
  title="The claim under test"
  kicker="What was published, and by whom"
  current="claim"
  lede="The idea is that a single satellite radar image, reprocessed as a set of sub-apertures, holds the vibration of the ground, and that the vibration can be focused into a picture of what lies hundreds of metres beneath it. This page keeps apart the four things that are easily blurred: the published claims, the public protocol derived from them, this lab's own work, and the difference between simulation and measurement."
  index={[
    { id: 'timeline', label: 'Timeline' },
    { id: 'published', label: 'Published claims' },
    { id: 'protocol', label: 'Replications' },
    { id: 'ours', label: 'This lab' },
    { id: 'honesty', label: 'Simulated and measured' },
  ]}
>
  <section id="timeline">
    <h2>Four years from the method to its retraction</h2>
    <Timeline />
  </section>

  <section id="published">
    <h2>The method was published in 2022 and retracted in 2026</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="note-card">
        <span class="tag claimed">claimed</span>
        <h3>Single-image <Term k="doppler-tomography">Doppler tomography</Term></h3>
        <p>
          Biondi and Malanga described the method in 2022, applied to the Great Pyramid
          (<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.00811">arXiv:2208.00811</a>). The paper was retracted by <em>Remote
          Sensing</em> on 10 August 2026 (<a href="https://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/18/16/2679">retraction notice</a>).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="note-card">
        <span class="tag claimed">claimed</span>
        <h3>The Khafre announcement</h3>
        <p>
          At a briefing in Bologna on 15 March 2025, the Khafre Project described eight vertical structures reaching more
          than 2,000 feet beneath the pyramid and further structures near 4,000 feet. The claim has not appeared in a
          peer-reviewed paper. Its geometry, as far as it was stated, is placed in the ground in
          <a href={`${base}/underworld/#bench-khafre-claim`}>the claimed underworld</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="protocol">
    <h2>Replications reconstruct the method, with choices of their own</h2>
    <p class="sub">
      Since 2025 the method has been reconstructed from its paper by others, filling missing details with choices of
      their own. This lab tests the method as published and the general idea behind it, and keeps any reconstruction's
      choices apart from the original's. Where a reconstruction adds stricter selection before its depth focus, the lab
      runs it unchanged beside controls: <a href={`${base}/satellite/#gates`}>motionless copies of the image pass its gates
      as often as the real one</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ours">
    <h2>This lab reimplements, simulates and measures, and says which is which</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="note-card">
        <span class="tag measured">the first investigation</span>
        <h3>The published pipeline on real dwells</h3>
        <p>
          Reimplemented as described, tested on scenes with known contents, and run on two ICEYE Spotlight Dwell products
          over Giza and Sacsayhuamán. <a href={`${base}/archive/`}>The full record is archived.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="note-card">
        <span class="tag simulated">underworld</span>
        <h3>Known ground, simulated instruments</h3>
        <p>
          Seismic arrays and the satellite over the same compositions, so the radar is judged against the best ground
          instruments on identical ground. The answer: the ground instruments find the chamber, the satellite cannot.
          <a href={`${base}/pictures/`}>In pictures</a> · <a href={`${base}/satellite/`}>The satellite</a> ·
          <a href={`${base}/seismic/`}>The ground</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="honesty">
    <h2>Every figure says whether it is simulated or measured</h2>
    <div class="honesty">
      <span class="tag simulated">simulated</span><span>computed over a composition whose contents are known</span>
      <span class="tag measured">measured</span><span>computed from a real acquisition</span>
      <span class="tag claimed">claimed</span><span>stated by others, placed as stated, never treated as found</span>
      <span class="tag planned">planned</span><span>designed, not yet run</span>
    </div>
  </section>
</Doc>

<style>
  .honesty {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: 10px 16px;
    align-items: center;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--body);
  }
</style>
